Original opt-in Wine 11 x64 native-thread start boundary. LGPL-2.1-or-later.

Apply after d3dmetal-wine-11.0-non-native-regions.patch and
 d3dmetal-wine-11.0-native-import-abi.patch, over the same reviewed Wine 11
 baseline. This contains original Caskrun code only, with no Apple or
 CrossOver implementation and no manual GS/TSD/signal changes.

Only starts inside the explicitly opted-in support dylib's already validated
executable __TEXT range are selected, and WoW64 is excluded. Preserve the
original start for server_init_thread and in the existing thread_data fields;
only the entry handed to normal signal_start_thread becomes our own resolved
PE relay. Missing paired PE relay fails explicitly, never calls NULL or falls
back to the broken direct native start. Default and outside-range starts keep
Wine's ordinary route. No additional heap/TLS allocation is used.

The relay returns through unchanged BaseThreadInitThunk/RtlExitUserThread
semantics. Its appended owned Unix call obtains and rechecks the current
thread's original start/argument, then invokes the typed Microsoft-ABI native
callback through Wine's ordinary native transition. The caller cannot supply
an alternate start pointer. Prior Unix indices are retained; the new WoW64
entry refuses support. The private x64 PE export is appended at the end of
ntdll.spec so existing auto-assigned export ordinals remain unchanged.

Build the matching NTDLL PE and native halves together. This experiment is not
an accepted runtime capability and has no Apple factory or game claim until
independent ordinary-PE/native-thread and combined graphics gates pass.

